<title>UK: GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greg Norman remains top of the</p>
<p>world rankings issued on Tuesday following his joint second</p>
<p>place in the Memorial Tournament in Ohio at the weekend.</p>
<p>Tournament winner Vijay Singh of Fiji joins the leaders in</p>
<p>20th spot while Briton Ian Woosnam, sudden-death playoff winner</p>
<p>of South Korea's Hyundai Motor Masters, moves up one place to</p>
<p>19th.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>  1. Greg Norman (Australia)	 10.35 points average</p>
<p>  2. Tiger Woods			  9.79</p>
<p>  3. Tom Lehman			   9.41</p>
<p>  4. Steve Elkington (Australia)    9.15</p>
<p>  5. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	    8.87</p>
<p>  6. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)    8.44</p>
<p>  7. Ernie Els (South Africa)	 8.41</p>
<p>  8. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	    8.27</p>
<p>  9. Mark O'Meara			 7.67</p>
<p> 10. Phil Mickelson		     7.12</p>
<p> 11. Fred Couples			 6.74</p>
<p> 12. Brad Faxon			   6.73</p>
<p> 13. Nick Faldo (Britain)	     6.72</p>
<p> 14. Scott Hoch			   6.67</p>
<p> 15. Davis Love			   5.84</p>
<p> 16. Bernhard Langer (Germany)	5.82</p>
<p> 17. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)	 5.76</p>
<p> 18. Steve Jones			  5.75</p>
<p> 19. Ian Woosnam (Britain)	    5.48</p>
<p> 20. Vijay Singh (Fiji)		 5.28</p>
</text>
